      "problem": "Consider a $6\\times 8$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=2,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =8 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
